{"id":"convexfeld-vk8l","title":"P1: helpers.c bound propagation is dead code — tautological comparison","description":"Code smell audit found src/solver_state/helpers.c:117-127 has a logic bug that makes the entire bound propagation body dead code:
  double newLB = lb_working[colIdx];
  if (newLB > lb_working[colIdx] + BOUND_TOL) { ... }
newLB was just assigned from lb_working[colIdx], so the comparison is always false. Same tautology for newUB at ~line 150. The propagated bound values need to be COMPUTED from constraint data and the coeff variable before comparison, not read from the same array.
Fix: Compute the actual implied bounds from constraint activities before comparing.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"tobias.osborne@itp.uni-hannover.de","created_at":"2026-02-23T17:23:57Z","created_by":"tobiasosborne","updated_at":"2026-02-23T17:23:57Z"}

{"id":"convexfeld-tyr8","title":"[specv2] Incomplete NaN/Inf detection after FTRAN/BTRAN (N7)","description":"**Audit finding:** The spec (numerical_stability.md Section C) requires NaN/Inf detection after FTRAN results. cxf_pivot_with_eta checks isfinite(pivot) for the pivot element only, but does not check the entire pivot column. FTRAN/BTRAN results are not checked for NaN/Inf in ftran.c or btran.c.

**Impact:** NaN/Inf values in non-pivot positions of the FTRAN result could propagate silently, causing hard-to-diagnose numerical failures downstream.

